tade hitotsu no

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.700
I only...

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.000
akogare dake wa

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.000
...have one desire

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.330
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.330
And no one...

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:34.260
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:34.260
...will ever take it away

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.230
episode

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.230
Is Something Going Down
\h       on Treasure Island?!

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:49.350
Listen everyone, the island you see there...

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.670
...is our final destination.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:55.900
During our voyage, we've done well to overcome a number of dangers.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.610
But our journey is far from over.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.390
The hardest part may still be ahead of us.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.540
So I'm expecting your best efforts.

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:10.430
Gentlemen, you have done excellent work.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.750
Tomorrow, we'll go to shore,

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.710
but tonight, we're going to put aside the usual strictness...

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.880
...and open a barrel of rum.
A big barrel!

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.130
You hear that?
Rum!

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.220
Yeah, it's been a long time.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.110
Cheers for Mr. Trelawney!

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.440
Hurray! Hurray!

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.150
S-Stop it, that's enough.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.900
And for Captain Smollett also.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.270
Hurray!

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:42.570
Hurray! Hurray!

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.830
Without further ado, gentlemen,
make this night worthwhile!

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.380
Fifteen men...

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:00.710
...on a dead man's chest!

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:05.360
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:13.210
Drink and the devil had done for the rest!

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:18.730
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.030
...on a dead man's chest!

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.700
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:39.630
Drink and the devil had done for the rest!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:44.490
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:50.930
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.690
Darn him!
How dare that crook toy with me!

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.820
I'll never believe another words he says!

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.850
No matter what he tells me!

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.400
Damn him!

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.200
Everything is completely over between us!

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.570
Shut up!

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.560
Leave me alone, Benbow!

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:12.220
There are times in life where we want to be alone!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.850
So leave me alone!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.310
Damn him... Damn him!
And to think I trusted him!

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:32.410
Silver had me convinced that he wasn't someone bad!

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.040
Damn him!

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:03.270
<i>And to think...</i>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.490
<i>To think he was part of a group of damned pirates...!</i>

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:08.820
Damn him!

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:12.070
Damn him!

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:14.660
Damn him!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.700
Damn him! Damn him!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.900
Hey, that's enough now.
You're going to catch a cold.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.050
We really can't leave you alone.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.430
Okay then, good night.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.070
<i>Damn him!</i>

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.770
<i>Damn him! Damn him!</i>

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.320
<i>Damn him! Damn him!
DAMN HIM!</i>

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.150
<i>Damn him!</i>

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.200
Fifteen men...

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.710
...on a dead...

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:59.160
...man's chest...

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:03.550
Drink and the devil...

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.630
Anderson, have you seen Jim?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:09.100
No, I haven't seen him.
Yo-ho-ho!

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.260
Silver!

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.890
What is it?
You look sorta out of it.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.650
Get used to it.
I'll look like this a lot.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.480
Hey!

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:31.620
Come on, don't be like that.
Have drink with me, yeah?

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:32.860
Let go of me.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:38.170
Didn't you hear me? Take your filthy paw of my shoulder.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:49.430
W-W-Wait a moment, Silver.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.220
Silver, I have something to tell you.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.470
I'm not interested.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:56.800
Go away! Go away!

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.230
<i>Damn!</i>

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:21.830
Okay, in any case!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:26.830
I have to go talk to Mr. Trelawney
and Dr. Livesey about Silver.

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:42.390
It's Silver...

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:14.970
I-I'm trapped.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.570
Who's there?

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:58.570
It's Jim. I have something
very important to tell you.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:10:59.720
Come in.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.780
Okay.

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.850
So, Jim, what is it that's so important?

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:07.810
Yes, actually it's...

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.710
I refuse to believe it!
It's impossible!

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:33.270
Jim, I refuse to believe that Silver is a pirate...

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:36.440
...and that he's planning a mutiny. I'll never believe it!

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:39.270
Mr. Trelawney, calm down please.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:42.270
Jim had nothing do to with it.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:45.350
Jim's just telling us what he heard...

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.140
...when he was in the barrel.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.160
I-I know, but...

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:49.680
Mr. Trelawney,

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.350
Jim has shown a lot of courage by coming to tell us.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.120
I-I guess you're right...

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.620
I... I've let my guard down.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.670
During my career,

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:10.630
I've known crews to plan mutiny.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:13.110
There were always warning signs.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:16.420
But this time, I didn't notice anything.
It's all my fault.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.910
No, captain. The only one responsible is Silver.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:21.950
We've all been deceived.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:24.870
He planned everything before even embarking with us.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:27.890
Yes, Silver truly is a terrible man.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.900
In any case, we have to do something.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:36.590
Captain Smollett, forgive me
for being so hard on you before.

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:38.670
Don't you agree...

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:42.410
...that we must work together to crush this cursed Silver?

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.110
Count on me, Mr. Trelawney.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:51.040
With that decided, let's discuss our battle plans immediately.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:59.830
For starters, I'd like to explain two or three points.

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:01.350
First,

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:05.030
we must sail to the island as if nothing has happened.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.270
If I were to turn back,

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:09.600
Silver and his friends would strike immediately.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.570
Yes, that would likely be the case for a demon like Silver.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:19.470
Second, time is still in our favor.

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.630
At least until we discover the treasure.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.190
Isn't that right, Jim?

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.050
Yes, that's right.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.360
<i>As for our plan,</i>

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:31.250
<i>it starts by letting this idiot Trelawney lead us right to the treasure.</i>

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.580
<i>And then we'll get rid of them and split up the loot.</i>

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:39.000
Yes, that's definitely what they said.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:45.220
Concluding, allow me to finish this meeting with the most important point:

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.390
There may be some men...

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:50.800
...who haven't joined Silver and may still be faithful to us.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.770
We must find out who.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:54.730
That's essential.

00:13:55.670 --> 00:13:58.650
I see, but at the moment, there's only four of us:

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.190
Captain Smollett,

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.650
Dr. Livesey, Jim...

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.570
...and of course, myself.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:06.530
Besides us, there's also my servant,
Old Redruth.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.540
That makes a total of five.

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:15.630
That seems a bit small compared to Silver's twenty men.

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:18.500
Of course, there's also Joyce and Hunter!

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:20.170
Joyce and Hunter?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:23.310
They once worked with me.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:26.800
I hired them as sailors for this trip.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:30.340
Joyce! Hunter!

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.260
Th-That you, sir?

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:36.730
Come on, this way.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:40.870
Really?

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:44.350
So there's a mutiny planned on this ship, sir?

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:48.470
Understood, you can count on me!

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:51.410
Me too!
I will do my best to help you!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.870
Perfect, we're now seven.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:05.430
<i>Jim.</i>

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:09.590
<i>From now on, we will surely face terrible danger.</i>

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:12.470
<i>So you must be strong.</i>

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:17.690
<i>Jim, we must be strong.
This demon must not win!</i>

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:22.530
I don't have any intention of letting someone like Silver win!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:29.930
<i>S-Silver!</i>

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.740
<i>You won't catch me!</i>

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.190
<i>Damn it...!</i>

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.170
Jim!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.970
What is it?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:53.140
You look frightened.
Had a bad dream, my boy?

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:03.360
What, morning already?
I feel like I haven't slept at all.

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:20.900
What are you doing here?!

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:25.910
Even if you had permission to drink last night,

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:29.130
that doesn't mean you
can slack off on chores!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.770
Return to your posts this instant!

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:34.670
Yeah, yeah.
We were just about to go.

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:38.140
Really, you're very hard on us, captain.

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:43.430
Jim, soon we'll be on Treasure Island!

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:56.240
This island is so quiet.
It's like a cemetery.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.980
<i>A little while later,</i>

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:27.480
<i>heading to a place that the treasure map
indicated as "Skeleton Island",</i>

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:30.780
<i>we were in "The Bay of Captain Kidd".</i>

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:34.950
<i>Treasure Island, finally.</i>

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:46.060
Very good, drop the anchor!

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.740
It's Treasure Island!

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.740
Incredible!

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:58.140
You said it!

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.050
Jim!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.560
Jim!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.500
Listen to me carefully.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.580
The first team of reconnaissance will depart soon.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:15.580
Those who want to can join.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:18.380
Among them will surely be Silver and his men.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:20.500
I want you to accompany them, Jim.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:24.050
Good, the first team of reconnaissance is ready to depart!

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:33.020
<i>Jim, only you can carry out this mission.</i>

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:34.210
<i>We're counting on you.</i>

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:39.140
<i>The two boats of the first team of reconnaissance,</i>

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:41.020
<i>made their way to Treasure Island.</i>

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:47.060
<i>I deliberately didn't get into the boat with Silver.</i>

00:18:58.300 --> 00:18:59.200
We're counting on you, Jim.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.480
Once you arrive on the island,

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:10.620
follow Silver and his men quietly after separating from them.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.120
We're going to stay on board.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:15.380
They might take the chance to discuss the mutiny.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.520
So be extra careful now.

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:21.680
Take this with you in case of danger.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.840
We're counting on you, Jim!

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:39.030
Come on, Benbow.
Let's go!

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:43.910
Hey, Jim!
Wait!

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:46.370
We'll explore the island together!

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:50.330
I'm not going to wait!
I won't obey a pirate!

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.140
Say, boss.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:05.080
This island is huge. You have any idea where the treasure is?

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:08.380
Not a clue.
We'll start by exploring the area.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.760
That's why we volunteered in the first place.

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:12.220
Aye, understood.

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:16.690
Hey, Silver!
I wanna have a word!

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.570
I have to talk to you, Silver.

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:27.240
Go on, I'm listening.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.020
Up until now, you've been our leader,

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:33.210
but that course has run its end.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.340
We must have a new leader...

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:40.630
...and I've decided it'll be me.
Understand, Silver?

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:53.290
What are you laughing at, Silver?!

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:59.230
You can't decide all on your own. The others must agree.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.460
Don't worry about that.
They've already decided.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:08.670
They've all agreed that I'll be the new leader.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:09.600
Isn't that right, guy—

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:21.170
Wh-What's this?
You lot betrayed me?!

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.640
No, quite the opposite.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.590
The traitor here, is you.

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:29.350
Your time has come.

00:22:24.460 --> 00:22:27.610
<i>Silver really is a pirate...</i>

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:29.750
<i>A real pirate!</i>

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:32.040
To      be        continued

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:38.290
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:38.290
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:44.100
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:44.100
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:50.310
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:50.310
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.310 --> 00:22:55.750
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.310 --> 00:22:55.750
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.750 --> 00:23:01.160
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.750 --> 00:23:01.160
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:06.620
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:06.620
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:12.250
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:12.250
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:18.110
kakaete kaeritai

